<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">March of Treviso</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Marca Trevigiana, Trevisan March</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The March of Treviso was a medieval name for the region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> around Treviso, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicenza">Vicenza</a>, Feltre and Belluno, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> and the Venetian lagoon. Dominated by the da Romano family in the 13th century, it was known for its courtly culture as the Marca gioiosa. It was absorbed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>'s mainland territory from the late 14th century.</p></div>
